   "daf": "116a",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "אִם אָמַר לוֹ: ״אַצִּיל אֶת שֶׁלְּךָ וְכוּ׳״. אַמַּאי? וְנֵימָא לֵיהּ: ״מְשַׁטֶּה אֲנִי בָּךְ״!",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «if» the owner of the wine «said to» the owner of the honey: «I will salvage your» honey and you will pay me the value of my wine, the owner of the honey is obligated to give him compensation for the wine. The Gemara asks: «Why» is the stipulation binding? «Let» the owner of the honey «say to him: I was» merely «fooling with you» when I accepted your condition, and I did not agree to it at all."
  }
